# Plant scripts share ONE login that can only SEND (write) and listen to the "settings changed" ping and to the commands (cmd) for the plant.
# A command is signed by the cloud with the key of ITS gateway and carries an expiry time: another gateway or a replayed message is ignored.
# Every message is also signed with the key of the gateway named in its topic (each plant script has its OWN key),
# and the backend throws away anything not signed by that gateway or outside its State + Region, so one plant can
# never write into another company's - or another region's - data.
user stech_gateway
topic write stech/#
topic read stech/+/gw/+/config
topic read stech/+/gw/+/cmd

# The backend reads everything and sends the "settings changed" ping.
# V2.0: it also reads what customer gateways publish (JSON + Sparkplug B) and publishes the write commands to them.
# The customer gateways themselves are NOT in this file: each plant login is created live by the cloud (Dynamic Security
# plugin) and may only touch iview/<plant id>/# and spBv1.0/<plant id>/#.
user stech_backend
topic readwrite stech/#
topic readwrite iview/#
topic readwrite spBv1.0/#
